# signalFlow

ASCII call-thread wiring diagram renderer.

Takes a recursive call tree in YAML and produces a 2D diagram showing forward
calls (left → right) and returns (right → left) as a single continuous wire
through horizontally-arranged function chips grouped by module.

## Install

```bash
pip install -e .
```

## Usage

```bash
signalflow examples/show-cohort.yaml
signalflow -                    # read YAML from stdin
signalflow --example            # run built-in example
```

## Input format

```yaml
title: "my diagram"
tree:
  module: MyModule.ts
  func: "entry_point()"
  signal: '"input"'
  calls:
    - module: OtherModule.ts
      func: "helper()"
      signal: "arg"
      calls: []
```

